,"cat4":2,"cat5":3,"total":11,"comments":"Thank you for a great laste game ! "}],"spiritreceived":[{"game_id":16,"givenby":"Singapore Open","cat1":2,"cat2":2,"cat3":2,"cat4":2,"cat5":2,"total":10,"comments":null},{"game_id":17,"givenby":"New Zealand Open","cat1":2,"cat2":1,"cat3":2,"cat4":3,"cat5":2,"total":10,"comments":null},{"game_id":15,"givenby":"Australia Open","cat1":2,"cat2":2,"cat3":2,"cat4":2,"cat5":2,"total":10,"comments":"Some great call discussions and call retractions. \r\nSome 'hands' and arms in the stack. Physicality in the play was good but sometimes we thought the in the stack stuff was a bit much. "},{"game_id":111,"givenby":"Canada Open","cat1":2,"cat2":1,"cat3":1,"cat4":1,"cat5":2,"total":7,"comments":"It was a windy game which generally means more contact, however there were several examples of bids going through our players, and one bad jump into our player with position.\r\nThe discussions regarding contested calls were generally composed, but there was minimal consideration to our perspective. It felt like the default was to contest a call regardless of other perspectives.\r\nWhen these examples were brought to the attention of your team, there was laughter and a dismissive attitude."},{"game_id":110,"givenby":"Belgium Open","cat1":2,"cat2":2,"cat3":2,"cat4":2,"cat5":2,"total":10,"comments":null},{"game_id":107,"givenby":"Great Britain Open","cat1":2,"cat2":2,"cat3":3,"cat4":3,"cat5":3,"total":13,"comments":null},{"game_id":165,"givenby":"Italy Open","cat1":2,"cat2":2,"cat3":2,"cat4":2,"cat5":2,"total":10,"comments":null},{"game_id":175,"givenby":"Australia Open","cat1":2,"cat2":2,"cat3":2,"cat4":2,"cat5":2,"total":10,"comments":null},{"game_id":179,"givenby":"Belgium Open","cat1":2,"cat2":0,"cat3":2,"cat4":2,"cat5":2,"total":8,"comments":"Didn’t adapted the contacts despite many reminders for some players, especially number 8 and 57. "},{"game_id":182,"givenby":"Canada Open","cat1":2,"cat2":2,"cat3":2,"cat4":2,"cat5":3,"total":11,"comments